// @emit-error emitProgram: struct field type `u8[]` has no struct-field rep
// THE GENERIC-ALIAS HALF of `arrays/error-u8-struct-field-unsupported.vl`, which was
// CHECK-CLEAN INVALID WASM. The two files pin the SAME sentence on purpose: one field, two
// spellings, and the only thing that may distinguish them is which one a reader typed.
//
//   type W = { v: u8[] }        const b: W = { v: [7] }         — the direct spelling
//   type Box<T> = { v: T }      const b: Box<u8[]> = { v: [7] } — this file
//
// A `u8[]` STRUCT FIELD IS DEFERRED (#1805 shipped the packed byte list for the VALUE
// positions and left every CONTAINER position to its own kind ladder), and the direct
// spelling has refused in one line since. Through the alias INSTANCE the same field was
// silent, because the two spellings are interned by two different loops:
//
//   * `collectS`'s declared-struct loop codes the field with `fieldTypeCode` and emitFails
//     on -1 — the loud line;
//   * `gaeEnsure` codes the SUBSTITUTED field spelling with `nameFieldCode`, reads the same
//     -1, and RETURNS QUIETLY, leaving the instance un-interned.
//
// Quiet is correct for almost every -1 `gaeEnsure` sees — an un-interned field type is a
// PASS-ORDER answer a later pass improves, and three corpus files compile only because of
// it (`generic-application-name-grammar`, `nested-application-close-continuation`,
// `recursive-generic-alias-uninstantiated`). It was wrong for the DEFERRED kind, which no
// later pass improves. `fieldTypeIsDeferred` is the set that tells the two apart.
//
// WHAT THE SILENCE COST. With no row under `Box<u8[]>`, the binding's object literal fell
// to `collectAnonShapes`, which minted a `#anon` row from the LITERAL's syntax: `[7]` is
// all i32-range digits, so the field interned as an i32-list wrapper `(ref $lTypeIdx)` over
// what every read of `b.v` then treats as the packed one-byte backing. `vl check` said
// "no errors"; `vl check --codegen` said "the emitted module is not valid wasm ... expected
// (ref null $type), found (ref $type)".
type Box<T> = { v: T }

const b: Box<u8[]> = { v: [7] }
b.v = [255]
print(b.v[0])
